as follows:
1.
Grant. For and in consideration of One ThousandFiftv-Eight Dollars and No Cents
($1058.00) and other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are
hereby acknowledged, Grantor hereby grants and conveys unto Grantee, and its agents and
contractors, a temporary easement for construction purposes in connection with the construction
of Christensen Road (“Easement Rights”), located within the area depicted in the attached Exhibit
A and described as follows:
A portion of Tract 27, Foster Tracts, Laramie County, Wyoming,
more particularly described as follows:
Beginning at a point on the east line of Tract 27, from which the
southeast corner thereof bears S.00°06’56”W.. a distance of 404.18
feet; thence N.89°53’04”W., a distance of 113.61 feet; thence,
N00°06’56”E, a distance of 150.74 feet; thence N65°20’49”E, a
distance of 125.12 feet to the east line of Tract 27; thence
S.00°06’56”W., along the east line, a distance of 203.16 feet to the
point of beginning. Containing 20,102 square feet, more or less.
2.
Additional
Consideration.
As
additional
consideration
for
the
temporary
construction easement, the Grantee agrees to construct an approach to Christensen Road, described
as follows.
It is mutually understood and agreed that the Grantor currently has an access to his
land through a gate located on the boundary of the right-of-way of Christensen Road. Grantee
will, at its expense, move the gate and access to another location on Grantor’s land adjacent to
Christensen Road to replace the access point currently located on Grantor’s property and the
Christensen Road right-of-way.
The Grantor hereby grants to the Grantee permission to enter
upon Grantor’s adjacent land beyond the right-of-way line to construct, taper, and blend the
approach, install the gate and connect existing trails, roads, or lands, as depicted at Exhibit A.
3.
Use.
The Grantor hereby grants to Grantee and its agents and contractors, said
temporary’ construction easement area, as described above and depicted in Exhibit A, attached
hereto and incorporated as if fully set forth, such use to include the right of ingress and egress, and
also the right to temporaily operate equipment upon the above described land.
4.
Term. The permission granted herein shall become effective upon the issuance of
a Notice to Proceed pursuant to the general contract for the construction of the Christensen Road
overpass and Corridor and said permission shall remain in full force and effect for a period of two
(2) years thereafter.
