### Page 2 of 6

```text
5.
Maintenance Provision.
Grantee shall be responsible for all maintenance of the
temporary construction easement area during its use and shall restore the temporary construction
easement area to a condition equal to its state before its use the purposes identified herein.
Consistent with this restoration plan, upon completed use of the temporary construction easement
area, the disturbed area will be sloped, blended, and seeded or sodded, by the City to restore the
temporan construction area to a condition equal to its state before its use the purposes identified
herein.
6.
Miscellaneous.
Except for enforcement of the terms and conditions of this
Agreement as between the Parties, the Grantee reserves all immunities and defenses available
under the Wyoming Governmental Claims Act, W.S. § 1-39-101, et seq., and other applicable
laws. This Agreement is not intended to bestow third party beneficiary rights on any person or
entity not a party to this instrument. This instrument is governed by the laws of the State of
Wyoming and any disputes relating to this instrument shall be brought only in a court of competent
jurisdiction sitting in Laramie County, Wyoming.
TO HAVE AND TO HOLD the easement rights described herein unto the Grantee,
Grantee’s legal representatives, agents, and contractors, for the term described herein.
